    {
      "id": "p0137-b004",
      "kind": "quote",
      "source": {
        "text": "Those two married dogs always put presents under the tree for each other. It's always the same. A single bone. But every time, they act like it's the first time they've gotten it. Then Papyrus comes to take his bones back. Anyway, where are those two. .. ?",
        "raw": "Those two married dogs always put presents under the tree for each other.\nIt's always the same. A single bone. But every time, they act like it's the first\ntime they've gotten it. Then Papyrus comes to take his bones back. Anyway,\nwhere are those two. .. ?",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.13679768,
          0.29725714,
          0.70428571,
          0.36552857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.13547173,
          0.29654286,
          0.70561167,
          0.3666
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          16,
          17,
          18,
          19
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "那对狗夫妻总在树下给彼此放礼物。每次都只是一根骨头，却每次都表现得像头一回收到似的。然后 Papyrus 就来把骨头捡走。话说，那两个去哪儿了？",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
