    {
      "id": "p0137-b006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In English, we usually count objects by giving a number followed the name of the object: two dogs, 420 cats, seven farts. Sometimes, though, we use special \"counter words\" to count objects or groups of objects: three \"heads\" of!ettuce, a \"n1urder\" of crows, a \"tank\" of gas.",
        "raw": "In English, we usually count objects by giving a number followed the name of\nthe object: two dogs, 420 cats, seven farts. Sometimes, though, we use special\n\"counter words\" to count objects or groups of objects: three \"heads\" of!ettuce, a\n\"n1urder\" of crows, a \"tank\" of gas.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.08606463,
          0.42605,
          0.70524448,
          0.49355
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.0840247,
          0.42533571,
          0.70739661,
          0.49462143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          22,
          23,
          24,
          25
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "英语中，通常用数字加名词就能计数，比如“two dogs”（两只狗）、“420 cats”（420 只猫）、“7 farts”（7 个屁）。有时也会用类似量词的表达，如三“棵”生菜（three heads of lettuce）、一“群”乌鸦（a murder of crows）、一“箱”汽油（a tank of gas）。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
