    {
      "id": "p0137-b010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In the earliest drafts of the Japanese script, the translator chose hiki when referring to Dogamy and Dogaressa. Another team member later argued for using nin instead, given that they act overall more like people than dogs. The translator agreed and changed every instance of hiki to nin ... but accidentally missed one. As a result, the bear refers to the dogs as people and as small animals in the final draft of the Japanese script.",
        "raw": "In the earliest drafts of the Japanese script, the translator chose hiki when\nreferring to Dogamy and Dogaressa. Another team member later argued for\nusing nin instead, given that they act overall more like people than dogs. The\ntranslator agreed and changed every instance of hiki to nin ... but accidentally\nmissed one. As a result, the bear refers to the dogs as people and as small\nanimals in the final draft of the Japanese script.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09353077,
          0.79386429,
          0.68526337,
          0.8989
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.0840247,
          0.79315,
          0.70739661,
          0.89997143
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          40,
          41,
          42,
          43,
          44,
          45
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "最早的译稿用了“匹”。后来，有位团队成员认为它们更像人，应该用“人”。团队于是作了替换，却漏改了一处。最终版里，这只熊既把它们当作人来数，也把它们当作小动物来数。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
